# Order is important, the last matching pattern takes the most precedence.
#
# Each rule lists @DataDog/rum-browser and the team that owns the code: an approval from either is enough.
# Rule: code specific to RUM goes to Capture & Explore or Ecosystems, code for the whole SDK goes to CO-OP.

# SDK foundation — CO-OP (default: browser-core, js-core, browser-logs, worker, tooling, CI, e2e infra, dev extension, remote config)
*    @Datadog/rum-browser @DataDog/rum-browser-co-op

# RUM product — Capture & Explore (views, actions, errors, resources, vitals/operations, long tasks, websockets, RUM boot/config/assembly)
packages/browser-rum-core/**                   @Datadog/rum-browser @DataDog/rum-browser-capture-explore
packages/browser-rum/**                        @Datadog/rum-browser @DataDog/rum-browser-capture-explore
packages/browser-rum-slim/**                   @Datadog/rum-browser @DataDog/rum-browser-capture-explore
test/e2e/scenario/rum/**                       @Datadog/rum-browser @DataDog/rum-browser-capture-explore

